Subject: [A14 platform 05/18] hpd irq containment

Extracted mechanically from Python rewrite 5 in the tested postPatch recipe.
No resulting source changes; existing diagnostics and workarounds are retained.
Apply in the order in kernel/a14-post-patch.nix, after its DT appends.
The existing bank0 patch remains between platform patches 09 and 10.

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c
@@ -365,6 +365,23 @@
 	typec_switch_set(alt_port->typec_switch, alt_port->orientation);
 
 	/*
+	 * ASUS A14 diagnostic workaround: this kernel cannot pass IRQ_HPD
+	 * separately from a real connector hotplug. Suppress IRQ-only
+	 * notifications on the observed external-DP port while preserving
+	 * HPD-high plug and HPD-low unplug notifications.
+	 */
+	if (alt_port->index == 1 &&
+	    alt_port->svid == USB_TYPEC_DP_SID &&
+	    alt_port->hpd_state &&
+	    alt_port->hpd_irq) {
+		dev_info_ratelimited(altmode->dev,
+			"A14-DP: suppressing port 1 IRQ-only HPD notification\n");
+		pmic_glink_altmode_request(altmode, ALTMODE_PAN_ACK,
+					    alt_port->index);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	/*
 	 * MUX_CTRL_STATE_DP4LN/USB3_DP may only be set if SVID=DP, but we need
 	 * to special-case the SVID=DP && mux_ctrl=NO_CONN case to deliver a
 	 * HPD notification
